From: OpenWrt RTL8197F bringup <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: realtek: force R4K timer for RTL8197F

RTL8197F uses the MIPS CP0 Count/Compare timer for early bring-up.  The
subtarget config may request CONFIG_CEVT_R4K/CONFIG_CSRC_R4K, but those are
hidden MIPS Kconfig symbols and must be selected by the platform symbol to be
robust across oldconfig/syncconfig runs.

Without this, boot can reach plat_time_init(), print the RTL8197F R4K timer
message, and still fall back to the generic 100 Hz jiffies sched_clock before
hanging around delay calibration because no real clockevent was registered.
---
--- a/arch/mips/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/mips/Kconfig
@@ -974,6 +974,8 @@ config RTL8197F
 	bool "Realtek RTL8197F based platforms"
 	depends on MACH_REALTEK_RTL
 	select MIPS_EXTERNAL_TIMER
+	select CEVT_R4K
+	select CSRC_R4K
 	select CPU_SUPPORTS_CPUFREQ
 	select SYS_SUPPORTS_LITTLE_ENDIAN
 
